.TH WHAT-CHANGED 1 "September 2026" "what-changed 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
what-changed \- capture and compare privacy-conscious Linux system snapshots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B what-changed capture -o FILE
[--category NAME] [--exclude NAME] [--track PATH] [--include-transient]
.br
.B what-changed compare BEFORE AFTER
[--format text|json|markdown] [--include-transient]
.br
.B what-changed show FILE
[--format text|json|markdown]
.br
.B what-changed validate FILE
.br
.B what-changed categories
.SH DESCRIPTION
Captures curated read-only observations and reports semantic differences. A reported change is not a claim of causality. Unavailable collection is not treated as removal.
.SH PRIVACY
Defaults omit hostnames, users, addresses, machine IDs, UUIDs, serials, secrets, environment variables, and configuration contents. Tracked regular files are represented by metadata and SHA-256. Symlinks are not followed. Snapshots are created mode 0600 and are never silently overwritten.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -o, --output FILE
New snapshot path.
.TP
.B --category NAME
Include a category; repeatable.
.TP
.B --exclude NAME
Exclude a category; repeatable.
.TP
.B --track PATH
Track an absolute configuration path; repeatable.
.TP
.B --include-transient
Capture or compare active systemd state, classified as contextual.
.TP
.B --format FORMAT
text, json, or markdown.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 2 usage; 3 invalid snapshot; 4 filesystem failure; 5 collection/runtime failure.
.SH FILES
/etc/os-release, /var/lib/dpkg/status, systemd unit directories, /proc/self/mountinfo, selected /sys entries, APT/YUM repository files.
.SH SECURITY
No shell is invoked. Optional rpm and systemctl reads use fixed paths, fixed arguments, bounded output, and timeouts. Inspect snapshots before sharing.
.SH AUTHORS
GuhsHosting.
